.TH ITHACA 1 "November 2026" "Ithaca 1.0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ithaca \- small music player for GNOME
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ithaca
[\fIOPTION\fR] [\fIFILE\fR|\fIFOLDER\fR|\fIPLAYLIST\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ithaca plays your music, and nothing else. Songs, folders and playlists
(.m3u, .m3u8, .xspf, .pls) given on the command line are added to the play
queue and the first one is played. If Ithaca is already running, they are
sent to the running instance.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ithaca/settings.json
Preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ithaca/queue.json
The play queue, restored with "Restore Playlist".
.TP
.I ~/.cache/ithaca/
Cover art and waveform caches.
.SH AUTHOR
